\section{Experimental Setup}
\label{sec:experimental-setup}

\subsection{Models}
\label{sec:models}

We conduct experiments on two 7B-parameter instruction-tuned models that share the Qwen2 backbone architecture (28 Transformer layers, 28 attention heads with 4-group GQA):

\paragraph{DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B} serves as our primary evaluation target. This model was distilled from DeepSeek-R1 \cite{deepseek-r1} and produces explicit chain-of-thought traces delimited by \texttt{<think>}$\cdots$\texttt{</think>} tags, yielding sequences with pronounced phase structure---extended reasoning followed by a concise solution. The structured generation pattern makes it well-suited for studying how sparsity interacts with distinct reasoning phases.

\paragraph{Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct} \cite{qwen2.5} provides a cross-model replication. Although it shares the same backbone family, its instruction tuning does not enforce explicit reasoning delimiters, producing a different distribution of attention sparsity across the generation trajectory. Replication on this model tests whether our findings generalize beyond distillation-induced phase structure.

Both models are loaded in \texttt{bfloat16} precision with eager attention (i.e., without FlashAttention) to permit direct manipulation of attention weight matrices during sparsity intervention.\footnote{An earlier \texttt{float16} configuration produced sporadic NaN values in Layer~27 of DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, affecting ${\sim}$8\% of logit positions. Switching to \texttt{bfloat16} eliminated all NaN occurrences; we additionally apply NaN-guarded filtering as a safety net.}


\subsection{Dataset}
\label{sec:dataset}

We evaluate on a 50-problem stratified subset of the MATH-500 benchmark \cite{math500}, sampling uniformly across problem categories (algebra, geometry, number theory, combinatorics, etc.) with a fixed seed for reproducibility. Mathematical reasoning tasks are a natural testbed for our study: they elicit long chain-of-thought sequences (up to 2048 tokens) in which the model alternates between exploratory reasoning and structured computation---phases that differ markedly in attention sparsity. Each problem is decoded greedily (\texttt{max\_new\_tokens}$=$2048) to eliminate sampling variance.


\subsection{Compound Sparsity Configuration}
\label{sec:sparsity-config}

We apply \emph{symmetric} compound sparsity: for a given sparsity level $s$, we prune the same fraction $s$ of attention heads and evict the same fraction $s$ of KV cache entries. We evaluate four sparsity levels $s \in \{0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30\}$, spanning from mild to aggressive compression.

